    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-14581" textLabel="MONOMER-14581" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q8H3P9" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="O-28, pujar">The high-affinity K(+) (HAK) transporter gene family of plant potassium transporters. Members of this family were found in plants, Fungi, and probably Amoebozoa, but not in Protista and Animalia. 27 potential HAK genes are present in the |FRAME: TAX-4530 &lt;i&gt;Oryza sativa&lt;/i&gt;| (rice) genome |CITS: [18810495]|. The OsHAK7 gene was isolated from rice as a cDNA. It is localized to plasma membrane. The gene was expressed in yeast and E.coli, and shown to be a high affinity transporter of K+ |CITS: [12376644]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="MONOMER-14581" />
